@page "/admin-settings"

<PageTitle>Admin Settings - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<PageHero Eyebrow="OPERATIONSFLOW / ADMINISTRATION"
          Title="Admin Settings"
          Subtitle="Admin Settings documents the Week 3 local/free configuration surface and the Week 4 production upgrade path for OAuth2, Microsoft 365, SharePoint storage, notifications, reporting, and deployment hardening."
          BadgeText="Local Auth Enabled"
          BadgeClass="of-badge of-badge-success">
    <Actions>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/user-roles">User Roles</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/technical-overview">Technical Overview</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/integration-overview">Integration Overview</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-primary" href="/document-library">Document Library</a>
    </Actions>
</PageHero>

<PurposeNote Title="Purpose" Icon="⚙️">
    <p>
        This page explains the configuration surface OperationsFlow needs for a local/free deployment and a future Microsoft 365 production deployment.
        Week 3 now includes SQL-backed local authentication. Week 4 will add Microsoft OAuth2 account linking and live Microsoft 365 integration.
    </p>
</PurposeNote>

<MetricGrid>
    <MetricCard Title="Current Mode"
                Value="Local SQL"
                Detail="SQL-backed users, password login, roles, and permissions."
                Icon="🖥️"
                Tone="success" />

    <MetricCard Title="Storage Provider"
                Value="Local"
                Detail="Files are stored under wwwroot/uploads for local proof."
                Icon="📁"
                Tone="info" />

    <MetricCard Title="Future Auth"
                Value="OAuth2"
                Detail="Week 4 target for Microsoft account linking."
                Icon="🔐"
                Tone="warning" />

    <MetricCard Title="Future Files"
                Value="SharePoint"
                Detail="Week 4 target for production document library storage."
                Icon="☁️"
                Tone="warning" />
</MetricGrid>

<GuidanceNote Title="Current boundary" Icon="⚠️" Tone="warning">
    <p>
        Week 3 is a local/free implementation. It includes local password login and role loading, but it does not yet include
        Microsoft OAuth2, real Microsoft tenant authentication, live SharePoint storage, production password reset, hosted deployment,
        backup policy, or retention/compliance sign-off.
    </p>
</GuidanceNote>

<TableCard Title="Current local/free settings"
           Subtitle="These settings describe the working Week 3 local foundation.">

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Setting</th>
                <th>Current Value</th>
                <th>Notes</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Application mode</span></td>
                <td>Local demo / portfolio prototype</td>
                <td>Used to prove the workflow and local/free deployment path.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Database</span></td>
                <td>SQL Server Express / LocalDB</td>
                <td>Stores workflow records, activity logs, attachment metadata, users, roles, and permissions.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Auth provider</span></td>
                <td>Local SQL</td>
                <td>Username/password login backed by LocalUsers.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Password storage</span></td>
                <td>Hashed passwords</td>
                <td>Passwords are not stored in plain text.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Session mode</span></td>
                <td>Persistent local login</td>
                <td>Browser stores local user id only; app reloads roles/permissions from SQL.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">File storage provider</span></td>
                <td>Local</td>
                <td>Files are stored locally under wwwroot/uploads.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Attachment metadata</span></td>
                <td>DocumentAttachment records</td>
                <td>Links files to module, record id, provider, file name, path/key, and status.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Activity audit</span></td>
                <td>Activity Log</td>
                <td>Upload/delete and workflow events are recorded for reviewer evidence.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-danger">Git safety</span></td>
                <td>Do not commit uploads or database files</td>
                <td>wwwroot/uploads, *.db, *.db-shm, *.db-wal, *.mdf, and *.ldf must stay out of commits.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</TableCard>

<div class="of-two-column-grid">
    <InfoPanel Title="Week 3 identity settings"
               Subtitle="The local/free version now has a real SQL-backed auth model."
               Tone="success">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Provider:</strong>
                <span>Local SQL authentication.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Users:</strong>
                <span>LocalUsers table.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Roles:</strong>
                <span>LocalRoles and LocalUserRoles.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Permissions:</strong>
                <span>LocalPermissions and LocalRolePermissions.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Session:</strong>
                <span>Persistent local login using saved user id, then SQL reload.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Logout:</strong>
                <span>Clears saved local user id and current in-memory user.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>

    <InfoPanel Title="Week 4 auth/settings needed"
               Subtitle="These settings support the move from local login to Microsoft OAuth2 linking."
               Tone="warning">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>OAuth2 provider:</strong>
                <span>Microsoft OAuth2 / Entra ID.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Tenant id:</strong>
                <span>Microsoft 365 tenant identifier.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Client id:</strong>
                <span>App registration id.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Secret/certificate:</strong>
                <span>Secure OAuth2 credential.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>External link:</strong>
                <span>Microsoft account maps to LocalUser through ExternalLoginLinks.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Authorization source:</strong>
                <span>Local SQL roles remain the application permission source.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>
</div>

<TableCard Title="Production setting groups"
           Subtitle="These are the major configuration groups needed for a production-ready OperationsFlow deployment.">

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Group</th>
                <th>Examples</th>
                <th>Production Concern</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Identity</span></td>
                <td>Local SQL users, Microsoft OAuth2 links, password policy</td>
                <td>Users need secure login and clear account ownership.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Authorization</span></td>
                <td>Roles, permissions, policy checks, admin-only areas</td>
                <td>Not every user should edit, delete, export, or manage settings.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Storage</span></td>
                <td>Provider, site id, drive id, folder convention, file limits</td>
                <td>Files must be stored somewhere supportable, permissioned, and backed up.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Audit</span></td>
                <td>Activity Log retention, login events, upload/delete events, record changes</td>
                <td>Operational systems need traceability for review and accountability.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Notifications</span></td>
                <td>Teams/Outlook alerts, Power Automate flows, reminder schedules</td>
                <td>Production systems should push important follow-up work to the right people.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Reporting</span></td>
                <td>CSV exports, Power BI dataset, scheduled reporting</td>
                <td>Managers need repeatable review outputs, not manual screenshot hunting.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</TableCard>

<InfoPanel Title="Week 4 admin implementation path"
           Subtitle="Admin Settings should move from documentation into real configurable production behaviour."
           Tone="info">

    <div class="of-review-proof-grid">
        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 1</span>
            <h3>OAuth2 config</h3>
            <p>
                Add appsettings/user-secrets/environment variable support for Microsoft OAuth2 tenant, client, and callback settings.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Step 2</span>
            <h3>Account linking</h3>
            <p>
                Link Microsoft identities to existing LocalUser records through ExternalLoginLinks.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Step 3</span>
            <h3>Role policy config</h3>
            <p>
                Continue using local SQL roles/permissions as the app authorization source after Microsoft login.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Step 4</span>
            <h3>Deployment notes</h3>
            <p>
                Document the production values required before a real organisation could safely run the app.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</InfoPanel>

<GuidanceNote Title="Block 9 outcome" Icon="✅" Tone="info">
    <p>
        Admin Settings now reflects the upgraded Week 3 local/free authentication system and the Week 4 OAuth2/Microsoft 365 production direction.
    </p>
</GuidanceNote>